# npc_slayn — the outcome, not the verb.
#
# cli/verb/slay/ proves the chip is printed. This proves the chip corresponds to something
# real: the world is inspected before and after, and it moved. The two overlap on purpose —
# same scenario, different question.
#
# Slay and cut are Required verbs: the knife must be COMBINED with the action, not merely
# carried. It is the reference tool of both, so neither combination reaches the item critic
# (which picks at random under --playground).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --grant-item knife --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# --- before ---
inspect npcs
expect-state npcs brewer

strategy succeed
goal slay
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 1
regions
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions
click action 1
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180


# --- the outcome really ran ---
expect-outcome npc_slayn

# --- after: the world moved ---
inspect npcs
expect-no-state npcs brewer
quit
